 "result": "```python\n\"\"\"Step 11: the client's two requests as named entry points.\n\nfamilies() sorts builds into types by k-means clustering over the input (flag)\ncolumns only. best() returns the row indices of the builds that are not\nPareto-dominated on the goals, capped at 5% of rows. Both delegate to step1,\nwhich holds the implementations.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport step1\n\n\ndef families(train_csv) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return one family (cluster) label per data row of train_csv, in file order.\"\"\"\n    return step1.families(train_csv)\n\n\ndef best(train_csv) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return sorted row indices of the unusually good rows, at most 5% of rows.\"\"\"\n    return step1.best(train_csv)\n```",
